{"id":"530d893971fd0645140509b0df1765b64b9f882c","url":"https://fields-studio.arenaphysica.com/","title":"Atlas Fields Studio | Arena Physica","site_name":"Buzzing","source":"fields-studio.arenaphysica.com","byline":null,"excerpt":"Describe a design, simulate it, and watch the predicted electric and magnetic fields resolve.","content_html":"<DIV class=\"page\" id=\"readability-page-1\"><div id=\"field-content\">\n\n  <details open id=\"model-overlay-section\">\n    <summary>Field Source</summary>\n    <div>\n      <p><label>Model</label>\n        \n      </p>\n      <p><label>Ckpt</label>\n        \n      </p>\n      <div>\n        <p><label>Show</label></p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </details>\n\n  <details open id=\"querypoints-section\">\n    <summary>Query Points</summary>\n    <div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"q-sampling-rows\">\n        <p><label>Points</label>\n          \n          <span id=\"val-q-npoints\">10000</span>\n        </p>\n        <p><label title=\"Sampling region size: in-plane span = multiplier × board size; vertical span = half that. Centered on the board.\">Airbox ×</label>\n          \n          <span id=\"val-q-airbox\">4.0</span>\n        </p>\n        <p><label>Seed</label>\n          \n          \n        </p>\n      </div>\n      <div id=\"q-adaptive-rows\">\n        <p><label title=\"How far the cloud spreads off the metal, as a fraction of the airbox reach — larger fills more of the box, smaller keeps a tight skin on the conductors.\">Spread</label>\n          \n          <span id=\"val-q-spread\">0.10</span>\n        </p>\n      </div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </details>\n\n  <details open id=\"physics-section\">\n    <summary>Physics</summary>\n    <div>\n      <div>\n        <p><label>Field</label></p>\n      </div>\n      <p><label>Port</label>\n        \n        <label title=\"Highlight the excited port with a soft glow\">\n           Glow\n        </label>\n      </p>\n      <p><label>Freq</label>\n        \n      </p>\n      <p><label>Phase</label>\n        \n        \n        \n      </p>\n      <p><label>Speed</label>\n        \n        <span id=\"val-phase-speed\">3.00s</span>\n      </p>\n    </div>\n  </details>\n\n  <details open id=\"fieldrender-section\">\n    <summary>Field Render</summary>\n    <div>\n      <div>\n        <p><label><span>Quality</span><span>Render</span></label></p>\n      </div>\n      <!-- Render mode — Vectors uses the existing arrow primitives.\n           Streamlines re-integrates field lines per phase frame from the\n           voxelized scattered samples (animated geometry). -->\n      <div>\n        <p><label>Mode</label></p>\n      </div>\n      <!-- Far-field displacement slider — only meaningful when Far mode\n           is active. 0 = colored sphere, higher = bulgy antenna pattern. -->\n      \n      <p><label>Length</label>\n        \n        <label> Log</label>\n      </p>\n      <!-- Color by: built in JS via createLatexSelect so the option\n           labels render as math (|E|, E_x, E_y, E_z, φ). The shared\n           latex_select component handles the trigger/panel widget;\n           main.js owns the E/H/S option swap + the phi-disables-Log\n           sync. -->\n      <div>\n        <p><label>Color by</label></p>\n        <p><label id=\"lbl-log-color\">\n           Log\n        </label>\n      </p></div>\n      <!-- Slice locations. Colors each probe by the validation slicing axis it falls in, so a\n           per-slice metric in the report can be located in space. Options come from\n           /api/slice_labels (the server owns the axis list, not this markup). Clicking a\n           legend row isolates that bin. -->\n      <p><label>Slice by</label>\n        \n      </p>\n      \n      <p><label>Vec size</label>\n        \n        <span id=\"val-vec-size\">1.0</span>\n      </p>\n      <p><label>Stream size</label>\n        \n        <span id=\"val-stream-size\">1.0</span>\n      </p>\n      <!-- Streamline tuning (streamline / polarization modes). Pulse animates\n           direction-of-flow dashes. Stop at metal enforces the conductor\n           boundary. Density = number of seeds (magnitude-weighted, so lines\n           cluster where the field is strong); Log density weighting compresses\n           that bias. Grid res sets voxel resolution (detail, fixed footprint). -->\n      <p><label> Pulse streamline</label>\n      </p>\n      <p><label> Stop at metal</label>\n      </p>\n      <p><label> Log density weighting</label>\n      </p>\n      <p><label>Density</label>\n        \n        <span id=\"val-stream-density\">2048</span>\n      </p>\n      <p><label data-tooltip=\"Drop streamline seeds where |field| is below this percent of the field's peak (p95). Raise it to remove weak-field (e.g. off-board) lines — a probe for whether a spurious pattern is driven by the magnitude floor (lines vanish) vs direction noise (they persist)\">Seed mag floor</label>\n        \n        <span id=\"val-stream-seedfloor\">2.0%</span>\n      </p>\n      <p><label>Grid res</label>\n        \n        <span id=\"val-stream-grid\">128</span>\n      </p>\n      <p><label>Colormap</label>\n      </p>\n      <!-- Grid of gradient swatches — visual preview is the picker. The\n           active swatch gets an accent ring; clicking a different swatch\n           updates State.colormap immediately. -->\n      \n    </div>\n  </details>\n  </div><div id=\"geometry-content\">\n\n  \n\n  <!-- Cut the geometry with a plane of any orientation. The clip is a GPU material clip, so\n       scrubbing the plane is free; the cut outline comes from /api/zslice, debounced. -->\n\n  <p><label> Surfaces</label>\n  </p>\n  <p><label> Edges</label>\n  </p>\n  <p><label> Points</label>\n    \n    <span id=\"val-point-size\">4.0</span>\n  </p>\n  <p><label title=\"Ruler (M). Click any two entities — corners, edges, faces, via rims, mesh vertices — to dimension the shortest distance between them. One click alone reports that entity: edge length, face area, via diameter. Right-click undoes, Esc exits.\">\n       Measure\n    </label>\n  </p>\n  <p><label title=\"Show the S-parameter integration paths — V = -∫E·dl (ground→signal), I = ∮H·dl (loop around the signal) — plus the port-plane 2-D patch: sample points colored red=signal, blue=ground, and non-metal shaded by permittivity (grey air → teal substrate), with conductor anchors\">\n       Integral paths + patch (S-param)\n    </label>\n  </p>\n\n  <!-- Opening the expander IS enabling the cross-section: a disclosure that reveals a\n       checkbox you then have to tick is two gestures for one intent. The plane is always\n       axis-aligned, so the only ways to move it are the axis buttons, the offset, and\n       dragging its face. -->\n  <details id=\"xsec-section\">\n    <summary>Cross-section</summary>\n    <div>\n      <div>\n        <p><label data-tooltip=\"Which axis the plane cuts along — its normal\">Normal</label></p>\n      </div>\n      <p><label data-tooltip=\"Where the plane sits along that axis (mm). Dragging the cut in the viewport moves this\">Offset</label>\n        \n        \n      </p>\n      <p><label data-tooltip=\"Show only the cut face. With the geometry shown, everything above the plane is hidden so the cut is exposed\">\n           Hide geometry\n        </label>\n      </p>\n    </div>\n  </details>\n\n  <details id=\"densify-section\">\n        <summary>Densify<span aria-label=\"Beta feature\">BETA</span></summary>\n        <div>\n          <p><label>Face pts</label>\n            \n            <span id=\"val-densify-nface\">4096</span>\n          </p>\n          <p><label>Tet pts</label>\n            \n            <span id=\"val-densify-ntet\">4096</span>\n          </p>\n          <p><label>Seed</label>\n            \n            \n          </p>\n          <p><label> Area/volume weighted</label>\n          </p>\n          <p><label> Upsample pts</label>\n          </p>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n\n      <!-- Voxels mode controls (shown only when the Voxels geometry mode is active). -->\n      <div id=\"voxel-section\">\n          <p><label title=\"Fine voxels per axis — the geometry is rasterized into resolution³ cells.\">Resolution</label>\n            \n          </p>\n          <p><label title=\"Voxels per patch edge — patch³ voxels group into one patch; empty patches are dropped.\">Patch</label>\n            \n          </p>\n          <p><label title=\"Half-edge of the cubic region (mm), centered at the origin. Expanded beyond the ±4 mm board so E(3) augmentation can't push it out of the grid.\">Extent ±mm</label>\n            \n            <span id=\"val-vg-extent\">8</span>\n          </p>\n          <p><label title=\"Draw the fine voxels colored by material (copper metal / teal dielectric / red ports), not just the coarse patch boxes.\"> Show fine voxels</label>\n          </p>\n          \n      </div>\n\n      <details id=\"transform-section\">\n        <summary>Transform<span aria-label=\"Beta feature\">BETA</span></summary>\n        <div>\n          <p><label>Rotation °</label></p>\n          <p><label title=\"Yaw — rotation about z. Composed R_z·R_y·R_x, the same as training's so3 draw.\">Yaw</label>\n            \n            <span id=\"val-e3-yaw\">0</span>\n          </p>\n          <p><label title=\"Pitch — rotation about y.\">Pitch</label>\n            \n            <span id=\"val-e3-pitch\">0</span>\n          </p>\n          <p><label title=\"Roll — rotation about x.\">Roll</label>\n            \n            <span id=\"val-e3-roll\">0</span>\n          </p>\n          <p><label>Translation mm</label></p>\n          <p><label title=\"Translation along x (mm).\">X</label>\n            \n            <span id=\"val-e3-tx\">0.0</span>\n          </p>\n          <p><label title=\"Translation along y (mm).\">Y</label>\n            \n            <span id=\"val-e3-ty\">0.0</span>\n          </p>\n          <p><label title=\"Translation along z (mm).\">Z</label>\n            \n            <span id=\"val-e3-tz\">0.0</span>\n          </p>\n          <p><label title=\"Improper transform (mirror x): E→R·E while H→det(R)·R·H (axial, flips sign).\"> Reflect (mirror x)</label>\n          </p>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n  </div></DIV>","content_text":"Field Source Model Ckpt Show Query Points Points 10000 Airbox × 4.0 Seed Spread 0.10 Physics Field Port Glow Freq Phase Speed 3.00s Field Render QualityRender Mode Length Log Color by Log Slice by Vec size 1.0 Stream size 1.0 Pulse streamline Stop at metal Log density weighting Density 2048 Seed mag floor 2.0% Grid res 128 Colormap Surfaces Edges Points 4.0 Measure Integral paths + patch (S-param) Cross-section Normal Offset Hide geometry DensifyBETA Face pts 4096 Tet pts 4096 Seed Area/volume weighted Upsample pts Resolution Patch Extent ±mm 8 Show fine voxels TransformBETA Rotation ° Yaw 0 Pitch 0 Roll 0 Translation mm X 0.0 Y 0.0 Z 0.0 Reflect (mirror x)","fetched_at":"2026-09-02T14:16:31.562Z","ok":true,"blocks":[{"html_en":"<p><label>Model</label>\n        \n      </p>","sentences":[]},{"html_en":"<p><label>Ckpt</label>\n        \n      </p>","sentences":[]},{"html_en":"<p><label>Show</label></p>","sentences":[]},{"html_en":"<p><label>Points</label>\n          \n          <span id=\"val-q-npoints\">10000</span>\n        </p>","sentences":[{"en":"Points 10000","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p><label title=\"Sampling region size: in-plane span = multiplier × board size; vertical span = half that. Centered on the board.\">Airbox ×</label>\n          \n          <span id=\"val-q-airbox\">4.0</span>\n        </p>","sentences":[{"en":"Airbox × 4.0","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p><label>Seed</label>\n          \n          \n        </p>","sentences":[]},{"html_en":"<p><label title=\"How far the cloud spreads off the metal, as a fraction of the airbox reach — larger fills more of the box, smaller keeps a tight skin on the conductors.\">Spread</label>\n          \n          <span id=\"